        "description": "A scientist who studies the fundamental constituents and behavior of matter and energy.",
        "note": "The term 'physiciens' and 'physicists' in the context of Humboldt's work, especially in 'Kosmos', clearly refers to natural philosophers and early scientists who studied physical phenomena, which aligns with the modern concept of a physicist.",
        "wikidata_id": "Q169470",
