        "note": "The term 'heavens' in early modern texts encompasses both the religious concept of an afterlife destination and the physical realm of celestial bodies and space. 'Cosmos' best captures the latter, scientific sense, while the religious sense is more theological. Given the context with Humboldt, 'Cosmos' is the most fitting modern referent for the scientific interpretation.",
