        "wikidata_id": "",
        "wikidata_description": "family name",
        "wikipedia_extract": "December is the 12th and final month of the year in the Julian and Gregorian calendars. Its length is 31 days. December's name derives from the Latin word decem (meaning 10) because it was originally the 10th month of the year in the calendar of Romulus c. 750 BC, which began in March. The winter days following December were not included as part of any month. Later, the months of January and February were created out of the monthless period and added to the beginning of the calendar, but December retained its name. December is the first month of winter in the Northern Hemisphere and the first month of summer in the Southern Hemisphere."
