        "note": "The Portuguese 'dores dos olhos' directly translates to 'pains of the eyes', and the English 'sore eyes' refers to irritation or pain in the eyes.",
        "wikidata_id": "Q21077147",
        "wikidata_description": "medical symptom",
        "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eye%20pain",
        "wikipedia_extract": "Eye pain, also called ophthomalgia or ocular pain, is a nonspecific term for pain in one or both eyes, around the eyes, or behind the eyes. It may encompass minor eye irritation, aching, or burning sensation to intense and prolonged pain. Eye pain is a common complaint and a major driver of patient visits to both emergency departments and out-patient clinics, generally ophthalmology or neurology clinics. Between 2008 and 2019, there were 1 million emergency department visits and 4.6 million outpatient visits attributed to eye pain. Pain can occur in almost any part of the eye, including the eyelid, conjunctiva, sclera, cornea, or orbit (eye socket). Sensation of pain may be accompanied with swelling, throbbing or pressure, a stabbing or shooting pain, and/or the sensation of a foreign body in the eye."
