        "note": "'Amorphous substances' are a subset of inorganic or organic substances that lack a regular, ordered internal structure. However, in the context of contrasting with living substances or focusing on fundamental chemical constituents, 'inorganic compounds' is a fitting overarching term.",
        "wikidata_id": "Q190065",
        "wikidata_description": "compound that is not organic: i.e. does not contain carbon with exceptions e.g. CO, carbon dioxide, disulfide and diselenide, carbides, HCN, carbonic acid, cyanic, isocyanic and fulminic acids and carbonates, hydrogen carbonates, cyanides, cyanates",
