        "wikidata_description": "retarding force on a body moving in a fluid",
        "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Drag%20%28physics%29",
        "wikipedia_extract": "In fluid dynamics, drag, sometimes referred to as fluid resistance, also known as viscous force, is a force acting opposite to the direction of motion of any object moving with respect to a surrounding fluid. This can exist between two fluid layers, or between a fluid and a solid surface. Drag forces tend to decrease fluid velocity relative to the solid object in the fluid's path. Unlike other resistive forces, drag force depends on velocity. Drag force is proportional to the relative velocity for low-speed flow and is proportional to the velocity squared for high-speed flow. This distinction between low and high-speed flow is measured by the Reynolds number."
