        "note": "The text mentions 'B. Sachs' as a translator of Meynert's work and 'Sachs' as an author on the milk cure. Bernhard Sachs (1858-1898) was a neurologist and psychiatrist who translated Meynert's works. It is plausible this refers to him, though the 'milk cure' reference might point to a different Sachs, or a less prominent one.",
