        "note": "The term 'telescopic field of view' refers to the extent of the observable world that is seen through a telescope, which is a specific application of the broader concept of 'field of view'.",
        "wikipedia_extract": "The field of view (FOV) is the angular extent of the observable world that is seen at any given moment. In the case of optical instruments or sensors, it is a solid angle through which a detector is sensitive to electromagnetic radiation. It is further relevant in photography. In the context of human and primate vision, the term \"field of view\" is typically only used in the sense of a restriction to what is visible by external apparatus, like when wearing spectacles or virtual reality goggles. Note that eye movements are allowed in the definition but do not change the field of view when understood this way. If the analogy of the eye's retina working as a sensor is drawn upon, the corresponding concept in human (and much of animal vision) is the visual field."
