        "note": "The term 'electric heat' in the context of Somerville (1858) and Spencer (1862) refers to heat generated by non-natural, human-made processes, which can include electrical means, but also other forms of artificial generation. 'Artificial heat' is a more encompassing and appropriate modern term.",
